It captures BOTH NICs with tcpdump for every leg, so each leg self-verifies what was sent as
well as what was relayed; the scapy server's own record is a third, independent count.

dhcp4.py gained two things during this case, both generic and both in its README entry:
  --clients N / --gap S : N distinct clients (MAC and xid increment) in ONE process.
  bind_layers(UDP, BOOTP, dport=67/68) : see HARNESS FAULT 4 — without it a relayed frame is
  invisible to every scapy-based tool.

