OBSERVATION
================================================================================
O-3  `service dhcp-relay` on a device where relay is already enabled (the default) answers
     `% DHCP Relay is already globally enabled`. This is an ADVISORY — the requested state
     holds — but it is indistinguishable from a rejection to any driver that treats `% ` as an
     error, and `cfg.py` duly stopped its batch and skipped the remaining command. That is the
     documented `console.ADVISORY` class (tools/README.md, `console.py`), whose entries each
     cost a run. Offered as a candidate entry, with this transcript as the required evidence
     that the command took effect. NOT added mid-campaign: `console.py` is shared by every
     driver and changing it between cases of a live run is its own risk.

