================================================================================
VERDICT: PASS -- the DUT relays DHCP correctly in both directions: 5 of 5 crafted DISCOVERs and
their REQUESTs were forwarded to the configured server within 0.76 ms, with giaddr rewritten to
the client-side SVI 192.168.10.1 and hops incremented, and all 5 OFFERs and ACKs were delivered
back to the right clients. Both controls relayed exactly zero in the same configuration --
service disabled, and service enabled with no server address -- and the hop-count threshold is
enforced at its documented default of 10 (hops 2 relayed and counted to 3; hops 10 dropped).
Four harness faults were found and fixed en route, including one of standing value: a relayed
DHCP frame arrives from an ephemeral source port and so is not dissected as BOOTP by scapy
unless the tool binds on destination port alone.
